From: daurosk <354202035+daurosk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:41:06 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] build: the shader stamp script sets its CMake policies

Nx2ShaderStamp.cmake runs as "cmake -P", which sets no policies. On
CMake 3.x CMP0012 is then OLD, so while(TRUE) in hash_without_skip_blocks
is false and the FRITCHII_STAMP_SKIP blocks are hashed in: the stamp is
143af6f0d4195e81 (Linux, LF) instead of 3dc8b3ea00f9b392, and the build
stops. CMake 4 sets CMP0012 NEW by itself. The script now takes the
policies of the top-level cmake_minimum_required (3.31).
---
 CMakeModules/Nx2ShaderStamp.cmake | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeModules/Nx2ShaderStamp.cmake b/CMakeModules/Nx2ShaderStamp.cmake
index 73e0627118..2acc1620cd 100644
--- a/CMakeModules/Nx2ShaderStamp.cmake
+++ b/CMakeModules/Nx2ShaderStamp.cmake
@@ -22,6 +22,12 @@
 #   hashes: any later edit to these files leaves it, and the build stops again until someone
 #   checks that edit too.
 
+# A cmake -P script starts with no policies set. On CMake 3.x that leaves CMP0012 OLD: while(TRUE)
+# below is then false, the FRITCHII_STAMP_SKIP blocks are hashed in and the build stops on a stamp
+# no release carries (Linux LF: 143af6f0d4195e81 instead of 3dc8b3ea00f9b392). CMake 4 sets it NEW
+# by itself. The same version as the top-level cmake_minimum_required.
+cmake_policy(VERSION 3.31)
+
 set(SkipBlocksIn "vk_graphics_pipeline.h;vk_compute_pipeline.h")
 # v6.1, kept by 6.2: Windows (CRLF checkout), Linux (LF checkout).
 set(KnownStamps "143b6220486fb09b;3dc8b3ea00f9b392")
